# TypeScript

## Errors, config and telemetry

- Inside a module, throw an error. At a boundary (the services layer, a job
  handler, a route), return the failure as a value.
- One place maps each internal failure to a coded response of the product.
- Read `process.env` one time, at the composition root. Validate the values,
  give them types, and stop at startup when a value is missing or not valid.
  A secret has no default.
- Send telemetry over OTLP only. Do not import the SDK of a vendor. Connect
  the exporter of a vendor library to OTLP.

## Code

- Give an explicit return type to each exported function.
- Use `import type` for an import that gives only types.
- Do not use `any`. Use `unknown`, then narrow it.
- Use a named `function` declaration, not an arrow function, for a top-level
  function.
- Give one object parameter to a function with 3 or more parameters or with
  an optional parameter.
- Await each promise, or handle it and write a comment that tells why.
- Limit the concurrency of a fan-out. Decide if one failure stops all the
  operations, or if you collect all the results.
- Name a file `module.responsibility.ts`, for example `user.service.ts`. The
  name of a private folder starts with `_`.
- Use the `@/` alias inside a package. Do not use it across a package edge.
  Use a barrel `index.ts` only for a public surface.

## Tests

- Use Vitest with v8 coverage at 100%. Set the scope of the coverage with
  `include`. Do not decrease a threshold.
- Run the tests in sequence (`sequence.concurrent: false`).
- Put the code that only the tests use in `src/_testUtils/`.
- Run the tests through the scripts of `package.json`<% if has .all "pnpm" %> with `pnpm run`<% end %>, not
  with a bare `vitest run`.

## tsconfig

- Use three layers: `tsconfig.base.json` (strict), then `tsconfig.json`
  (`noEmit`, `@/*` to `./src/*`), then `tsconfig.build.json` (emit, no tests).
- The `check` script runs `tsc` with `tsconfig.build.json`.
- Set `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `noUnusedLocals` and `noUnusedParameters`
  in addition to `strict`.
- In `tsconfig.build.json`, set the `base-url` replacer of `tsc-alias` to off,
  so that it changes only the `@/*` paths.
- When an `@/` import fails at runtime, `tsc-alias` did not run on `dist/`.

Read `references/conventions.md` for the conventions, and
`references/local.md` for the own rules of this repository.
